    "body": "fix on issue/1152-electrode-body · PR #1811 · pinned by `a_rounded_pockets_faces_yield_an_electrode_whose_burn_is_judged_clean`, `the_same_electrode_in_a_smaller_cavity_is_convicted_as_a_gouge`, `a_cavity_that_is_no_rectangle_yields_a_body_electrode`, `a_sloping_sweep_is_bounded_from_both_sides_by_a_sampled_oracle` · merges at the next cut\n\nThe PR is a draft from the fork (`mkinney:issue/1152-electrode-body`, head 2f722e9c). The issue has the label `in-review`.\n\nWhat the PR does:\n- The stock sim has an outline atom (`stock_sim::simulate_outline`). It is exact at each column centre.\n- The electrode tool record has an `outline`. The project file, the tool library, `AddTool` / `ChangeTool` and the MCP tool definitions carry it.\n- `electrode_from_faces` makes a body electrode for a cavity that is not an axis-aligned rectangle. The refusal that named this issue is gone.\n- The size law of #543 judges an outline on its X and Y extents.\n- The field eye still refuses a program with an electrode (#548).\n\nWhat stays open, each refused by name today:\n- A wall picked as its welded (curved) face: #1808.\n- A drafted wall or a stepped floor: #1809.\n- A finish pass of a cavity with sharp corners that are not square to the axes (the size law refuses it as under size): #1810.\n\nNot exercised on a real EDM control. The conditions are synthetic.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
